{"title":"Pseudo-ring","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>pseudo-ring</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> that lacks a multiplicative identity.  In other words, it is a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> closed under two operations, addition and multiplication, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3cbabf73f39ebc4ea1a0a0c29037953b12f411a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(R,+)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Abelian_group\" title=\"Abelian group\">abelian group</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f552ab5e88d625e81ff4818903d41b5910af30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(R,\\cdot)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Associative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Associative\">associative</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Magma\" title=\"Magma\">magma</a>, and multiplication is doubly <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distributive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Distributive\">distributive</a> over addition.\n</p><p>By virtue of terrible pun, pseudo-rings are also called rngs (rings without i, the identity).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ideal\" title=\"Ideal\">Ideals</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisors</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiple\" title=\"Multiple\">multiples</a> may be defined as with rings.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Pseudo-ring&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pseudo-ring&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">Ring</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234658\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 34/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 525/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.985      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.985      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7017:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234658 and revision id 26505. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}